## Redis State Schema

All trade state is stored in Redis. There is no in-process locking — Redis is the single source of truth shared across threads.

| Key | Type | Value | Written by | Read by |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `trade:{trade_id}` | String (JSON) | Full serialised trade dict | `TradeChecker` | `TradeChecker` |
| `order:{order_id}` | String | `trade_id` | `TradeChecker`, `OrderManager` | `TradeChecker` |
| `{symbol}` | String | ISO timestamp (cooldown end) | `TradeChecker` | `TradeChecker`, `SignalAnalyzer` |
| `market_sentiments` | String | `"BULLISH"` / `"BEARISH"` / `"NEUTRAL"` | `Croner` | `SignalAnalyzer` |

> **Note:** Cooldown keys use the bare symbol string (e.g. `BTCUSDT`) as the key — not a prefixed form.

